Alt title: distinguishing between variables and metavariables.

If I say, in English "Surely you don't mean *x*.", it is clear (from
context) that "x" is a metavariable, standing in for a potential
expression, and not a variable bound to an actual expression.

Any suggestions on how to model that distinction in lojban?

